<h1>Tester Hub — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 25, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Tester Hub (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.testerhub</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Tester Hub holds <strong>zero permissions</strong> and makes <strong>no network calls</strong>. It collects <strong>no data</strong> — none. No accounts, no server, no analytics, no ads SDK, no tracking. It is a checklist that lives on your phone.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The app lists Useful Appz apps that are open for testing, with a one-tap opt-in button per app. Tapping a button hands that app's real Google Play link to your <strong>system browser</strong>, outside this app — Tester Hub never touches your Google account, and your actual testing sign-up happens on Google Play, under Google's own privacy policy. Only Google Play knows your real opt-in state; the app says so in its own screens.</li>
  <li>Your checklist — which apps you have marked as joined — is stored <strong>only on your device</strong>, in the app's own local storage. It never leaves your phone and is never visible to us.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>Only your checklist, on your device, as described above. We receive nothing, keep nothing, and sell nothing. Uninstalling the app erases the checklist.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>None.</strong> Tester Hub requests no Android permissions and makes no network calls.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>This version contains <strong>no ads and no advertising SDK</strong>. A box labeled "Ad space" appears in the app as a placeholder; it loads nothing and collects nothing. If a real ad integration ever ships, this policy and the app's Google Play declarations will be updated first.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Tester Hub is a tool for adults who test apps. It is not directed at children under 13, and it collects no data from anyone.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

